Goal: Design and build a small but real command-line application for managing recurring household tasks. The application must allow a user to: add a task; list tasks; mark a task complete; record when it was completed; identify tasks that are due again; persist data locally; include automated tests; include concise usage documentation. Select the implementation approach through the normal Howl workflow rather than pre-deciding the design. Deliver a working application demonstrable through its command line.
